														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1528372">
									

<p>How is that not what the Foundation expected it to do? They had established that the SCP works on the basis of 'Building + Cat = Entrails message'. That is <em>exactly</em> what happened in the the deviant tests. The contents of the message doesn't change the way in which the object functions, so there's no reason for an upgrade in class. Indeed, the only reason it acted up appears to be because people (the Foundation researchers) kept messing with it. If left alone (by cats), the object is apparently incapable of functioning anomalously.</p>
<p>This object passes the locked box test, and the unusual results don't change the fact that the effect can't occur if you don't feed this thing cats. For those reasons, it should be Safe.</p>

